## 3. LIVE BROADCAST DETECTION ENGINE

Implement real-time broadcast discovery.

Preferred integration:
YouTube Data API v3.

Use:
- channels.list to resolve channel handles to channel IDs.
- search.list with eventType=live and type=video to discover active broadcasts.
- videos.list to retrieve broadcast metadata and embeddability status.

Requirements:

1. Resolve and cache channel IDs.
2. Search for active broadcasts.
3. Associate broadcasts with the correct channel.
4. Retrieve video ID.
5. Retrieve title.
6. Retrieve thumbnail.
7. Retrieve publication/start information where available.
8. Retrieve channel name.
9. Check embeddability.
10. Cache results to minimize API quota consumption.
11. Refresh results on a configurable schedule.
12. Handle API quota limits.
13. Handle missing API credentials.
14. Handle deleted and private broadcasts.

Never mark a channel as LIVE simply because its streams page exists.

LIVE status must come from verified current broadcast information.

Use the following status categories:

- LIVE: verified active public broadcast.
- OFFLINE: no verified current broadcast.
- UPCOMING: scheduled upcoming broadcast.
- UNAVAILABLE: channel or API could not be checked.
- RESTRICTED: broadcast cannot be embedded.

Do not confuse API errors with OFFLINE status.

Provide an official YouTube fallback link for every channel.

Do not scrape YouTube pages as the primary live detection mechanism.

## 4. NEWS DASHBOARD DESIGN

Build a professional JARVIS News Center.

Visual design:

- Dark futuristic interface.
- Iron Man/JARVIS-inspired styling.
- Modern cards.
- Smooth animations.
- Responsive layout.
- High-quality thumbnails.
- Clear language indicators.
- Professional typography.
- Consistent with existing JARVIS design.

Main navigation:

NEWS CENTER
├── All News
├── Live Now
├── Hindi
├── English
├── Tamil
├── Telugu
├── Kannada
├── Malayalam
├── Bengali
├── Marathi
├── Gujarati
├── Punjabi
├── Favorites
├── Latest Videos
├── News Search
└── News Intelligence

Dashboard widgets:

- Total registered channels.
- Verified live broadcasts.
- Upcoming broadcasts.
- Offline channels.
- Favorite channels.
- Recently watched channels.

Do not show invented live counts.

## 5. LIVE TV PLAYER

Implement an integrated news player.

Features:

- YouTube embedded player.
- Play and pause.
- Fullscreen.
- Volume control.
- Playback state.
- Channel information.
- Video title.
- Original YouTube link.
- Related broadcast suggestions.
- Error handling.
- Responsive video layout.

When a broadcast is embeddable, play it inside JARVIS.

When embedding is disabled, open the original YouTube page.

Respect YouTube playback policies and copyright restrictions.

Do not download, extract or redistribute copyrighted live broadcasts.

Do not use unofficial stream extraction as the default playback method.

## 6. MULTI-CHANNEL NEWS WALL

Create a configurable multichannel viewing experience.

Support:
- Single-screen mode.
- Two-screen mode.
- Four-screen mode.
- Six-screen mode.
- Nine-screen mode.

Allow users to select channels for each panel.

Requirements:
- Each panel must have its own player.
- Only initialize players when needed.
- Allow individual fullscreen.
- Allow closing panels.
- Handle unavailable streams.
- Display actual channel names and status.
- Do not claim a channel is live without verification.

Use lazy loading to control resource consumption.

## 7. LANGUAGE FILTERING

Create a language selector.

Users must be able to choose any of the ten supported languages.

When a language is selected:

- Show only its registered channels.
- Show verified active broadcasts first.
- Show offline channels separately.
- Provide channel search.
- Provide favorites.
- Preserve the selected language.

Support an All Languages option.

## 8. NEWS SEARCH

Create intelligent news search.

Search by:
- Channel.
- Language.
- News title.
- Topic.
- Keyword.
- Broadcast availability.

Integrate accessible metadata from authorized sources.

Use the YouTube Data API where appropriate.

For general news headlines, optionally integrate Google News RSS and verified news publishers.

Clearly identify each article's publisher and original source.

Never invent news headlines or publication dates.

## 9. JARVIS AI NEWS ASSISTANT

Connect the News Center to the existing JARVIS voice assistant.

Implement dedicated AI tools:

- get_news_channels
- get_live_broadcasts
- get_channel_live_status
- open_news_channel
- play_news_broadcast
- search_news_videos
- get_latest_news_videos
- get_news_by_language
- add_news_favorite
- remove_news_favorite
- get_news_favorites
- summarize_news_content
- compare_news_coverage

Example voice commands:

&quot;JARVIS, open Aaj Tak live.&quot;

&quot;Play India Today.&quot;

&quot;Show all live Hindi news channels.&quot;

&quot;Open Kannada news.&quot;

&quot;Play TV9 Kannada.&quot;

&quot;Show all available Telugu news broadcasts.&quot;

&quot;Open four news channels simultaneously.&quot;

&quot;Which channels are currently live?&quot;

&quot;Show my favorite news channels.&quot;

&quot;Find the latest news about artificial intelligence.&quot;

&quot;Summarize the available headlines.&quot;

&quot;Compare how different news channels are covering this topic.&quot;

&quot;Stop the news.&quot;

&quot;Switch to Malayalam news.&quot;

The assistant must identify the requested channel and language accurately.

If multiple channels have similar names, ask for clarification.

Never report that a broadcast is playing before playback has actually started.

## 10. AI NEWS INTELLIGENCE

Create a news analysis engine.

Features:

1. Headline summarization.
2. Topic extraction.
3. News categorization.
4. Political news classification.
5. Business news classification.
6. Technology news classification.
7. Sports news classification.
8. International news classification.
9. Breaking news discovery.
10. Multi-source coverage comparison.

Use accessible articles, authorized metadata, captions where available and user-provided transcripts.

Distinguish:
- Verified facts.
- Publisher claims.
- Opinions.
- Unverified reports.

Attach source references to summaries.

Do not fabricate transcripts or claim to have watched a broadcast when only its title or description was available.

## 11. BACKEND ARCHITECTURE

Adapt to the existing JARVIS backend.

Suggested module:

backend/modules/news_intelligence/

    channel_registry.py
    youtube_api.py
    live_detector.py
    broadcast_discovery.py
    video_metadata.py
    news_search.py
    news_summarizer.py
    news_classifier.py
    favorites_service.py
    player_service.py
    news_agent_tools.py
    news_cache.py
    news_scheduler.py

Keep provider integrations independent.

Use background tasks for broadcast discovery.

Use Redis caching if already available in the project.

Do not introduce a conflicting backend framework.

## 12. DATABASE

Inspect the existing database and ORM first.

Suggested entities:

NewsChannel
- id
- name
- language
- youtube_handle
- youtube_channel_id
- streams_url
- logo_url
- enabled

NewsBroadcast
- id
- channel_id
- youtube_video_id
- title
- thumbnail
- status
- is_embeddable
- discovered_at
- last_checked_at

NewsFavorite
- id
- user_id
- channel_id

NewsWatchHistory
- id
- user_id
- channel_id
- video_id
- watched_at

NewsPreference
- id
- user_id
- preferred_languages
- autoplay_enabled

Use proper relationships and indexes.

Avoid storing unnecessary duplicated metadata.

## 13. API ENDPOINTS

Create endpoints following existing project conventions.

GET /api/news/channels

GET /api/news/channels/languages

GET /api/news/channels/{id}

GET /api/news/live

GET /api/news/live/{channel_id}

GET /api/news/broadcasts

GET /api/news/search

GET /api/news/latest

GET /api/news/favorites

POST /api/news/favorites

DELETE /api/news/favorites/{id}

GET /api/news/history

GET /api/news/analytics

All user-specific endpoints must require authentication.

## 14. ENVIRONMENT CONFIGURATION

Add required configuration to .env.example.

YOUTUBE_API_KEY=

NEWS_REFRESH_INTERVAL=300

NEWS_CACHE_TTL=180

NEWS_DEFAULT_LANGUAGE=all

NEWS_ENABLE_MULTI_VIEW=true

NEWS_MAX_PLAYER_COUNT=4

Never expose the YouTube API key in frontend code.

Validate configuration at application startup.

Handle missing API keys gracefully.

Use configurable refresh intervals and respect API quota limits.

## 15. TESTING

Test:

1. All ten language categories.
2. All 46 channel records.
3. Channel handle resolution.
4. Live broadcast discovery.
5. Offline detection.
6. Upcoming broadcast detection.
7. Embeddability.
8. Player opening.
9. Language filtering.
10. Search.
11. Favorites.
12. Watch history.
13. Voice command interpretation.
14. API quota failure.
15. Missing credentials.
16. Network failure.
17. Multi-channel player.
18. Responsive interface.
19. Unauthorized access.
20. Database persistence.

Use mocked API responses for automated tests.

Test actual YouTube API integration separately when a valid API key is configured.

## 16. DEVELOPMENT PHASES

PHASE 1: Inspect existing JARVIS architecture.

PHASE 2: Create the 46-channel seed database.

PHASE 3: Implement YouTube channel ID resolution.

PHASE 4: Implement live broadcast detection.

PHASE 5: Build the multilingual dashboard.

PHASE 6: Implement the video player.

PHASE 7: Implement multi-channel viewing.

PHASE 8: Implement news search and latest videos.

PHASE 9: Integrate JARVIS voice commands.

PHASE 10: Implement AI news intelligence.

PHASE 11: Complete testing and documentation.

## 17. ACCEPTANCE CRITERIA

The module is complete when:

- All 46 channel entries are registered.
- All ten languages work.
- Channels can be searched.
- Actual live broadcasts are discovered.
- Live and offline statuses are distinguished.
- Available broadcasts can be played.
- Non-embeddable broadcasts have an official fallback.
- Favorites work.
- Multi-channel mode works.
- Voice commands work.
- News summaries cite accessible sources.
- API failures are handled correctly.
- Existing JARVIS functionality remains intact.

## FINAL INSTRUCTION

Work directly in the existing JARVIS repository.

Do not create a mock-only dashboard.

Do not hardcode live status.

Do not fabricate broadcasts.

Do not expose API keys.

Do not replace existing JARVIS modules.

Implement each phase, test it, fix errors and document it.

The final goal is to make JARVIS a multilingual Indian news command center that can discover, open, play, search and intelligently summarize news from official news channel sources." data-testid="chatgpt-writing-block" data-writing-block-variant="document" style="--oai-wb-spacing: var(--spacing,0.25rem); --oai-wb-text-primary: var(--wb-text-primary,var(--color-token-text-primary,var(--text-primary,#0d0d0d))); --oai-wb-text-secondary: var(--wb-text-secondary,var(--color-token-text-secondary,var(--text-secondary,#5d5d5d))); --oai-wb-text-tertiary: var(--wb-text-tertiary,var(--color-token-text-tertiary,var(--text-tertiary,#8f8f8f))); --oai-wb-surface-primary: var(--wb-surface-primary,var(--color-token-main-surface-primary,var(--main-surface-primary,#fff))); --oai-wb-surface-secondary: var(--wb-surface-secondary,var(--color-token-bg-tertiary,var(--main-surface-secondary,#f5f5f5))); --oai-wb-interactive-secondary-hover: var(--wb-interactive-secondary-hover,var(--color-token-interactive-bg-secondary-hover,var(--oai-wb-surface-secondary))); --oai-wb-border: var(--wb-border,var(--color-token-border,var(--border-light,rgb(0 0 0/8%)))); --oai-wb-border-hover: var(--wb-border-hover,var(--color-token-border-default,var(--border-medium,rgb(0 0 0/12%)))); --oai-wb-divider: var(--wb-divider,var(--color-token-border-light,var(--border-light,rgb(0 0 0/5%)))); --oai-wb-focus: var(--wb-focus,var(--color-token-focus-border,var(--border-strong,#5b9dd9))); --oai-wb-control-border: var(--wb-control-border,var(--interactive-border-focus,var(--oai-wb-focus))); --oai-wb-entity-accent: var(--wb-entity-accent,var(--theme-entity-accent,var(--oai-wb-accent))); --oai-wb-accent: var(--wb-accent,var(--interactive-label-accent-default,#0285ff)); --oai-wb-on-accent: var(--wb-on-accent,var(--bg-primary,#fff)); --oai-wb-interactive-background: var(--wb-interactive-background,var(--interactive-bg-accent-default,color-mix(in srgb,#0285ff 12%,transparent))); --oai-wb-selection: var(--wb-selection,var(--theme-user-selection-bg,var(--selection,#93c5fd))); --oai-wb-radius: var(--wb-radius,1.5rem); --oai-wb-radius-sm: var(--wb-radius-sm,0.5rem); --oai-wb-shadow: var(--wb-shadow,0 4px 80px rgb(0 0 0/2%)); --oai-wb-shadow-lg: var(--wb-shadow-lg,0 10px 30px rgb(0 0 0/12%)); --oai-wb-font-sans: var(--wb-font-sans,var(--font-sans,sans-serif)); --oai-wb-font-mono: var(--wb-font-mono,var(--font-mono,monospace)); --oai-wb-font-size: var(--wb-font-size,0.875rem); --oai-wb-shimmer-dark-contrast: var(--wb-shimmer-dark-contrast,var(--oai-wb-text-tertiary)); --oai-wb-shimmer-dark-secondary: var(--wb-shimmer-dark-secondary,var(--oai-wb-text-tertiary));"><div aria-hidden="true" class="pointer-events-none absolute inset-0 rounded-[inherit] z-[-1] [background:var(--oai-wb-surface-primary)]"></div><div class="relative z-[1]"><header class="flex min-w-0 select-none items-center gap-[calc(var(--oai-wb-spacing)*2)] px-[calc(var(--oai-wb-spacing)*4)] py-[calc(var(--oai-wb-spacing)*2.5)] header-rXCNwJ sticky z-10 pe-2 pt-2 pb-2 [--wb-font-size:var(--text-sm)] !ps-0 !pe-2 !py-2" style="--oai-wb-spacing: var(--spacing,0.25rem); --oai-wb-text-primary: var(--wb-text-primary,var(--color-token-text-primary,var(--text-primary,#0d0d0d))); --oai-wb-text-secondary: var(--wb-text-secondary,var(--color-token-text-secondary,var(--text-secondary,#5d5d5d))); --oai-wb-text-tertiary: var(--wb-text-tertiary,var(--color-token-text-tertiary,var(--text-tertiary,#8f8f8f))); --oai-wb-surface-primary: var(--wb-surface-primary,var(--color-token-main-surface-primary,var(--main-surface-primary,#fff))); --oai-wb-surface-secondary: var(--wb-surface-secondary,var(--color-token-bg-tertiary,var(--main-surface-secondary,#f5f5f5))); --oai-wb-interactive-secondary-hover: var(--wb-interactive-secondary-hover,var(--color-token-interactive-bg-secondary-hover,var(--oai-wb-surface-secondary))); --oai-wb-border: var(--wb-border,var(--color-token-border,var(--border-light,rgb(0 0 0/8%)))); --oai-wb-border-hover: var(--wb-border-hover