="b47b8bf0-9151-4637-81cc-c27c479b2746 b47b8bf0-9151-4637-81cc-c27c479b2746"><h4 class="sr-only m-0 select-none print:not-sr-only print:mt-4 print:mb-2 print:text-xs print:leading-normal print:font-bold print:group-data-[print-formatting]/conversation-print:mt-6 print:group-data-[print-formatting]/conversation-print:font-normal print:group-data-[print-formatting]/conversation-print:text-secondary" data-conversation-role="assistant" tabindex="-1"><span class="print:group-data-[print-formatting]/conversation-print:sr-only">ChatGPT said:</span><span class="hidden print:group-data-[print-formatting]/conversation-print:inline" aria-hidden="true">ChatGPT</span></h4><div><div class="group flex min-w-0 flex-col" data-chatgpt-selection-conversation-id="6ae82d5d-c660-83ec-9016-d84695838fc0" data-chatgpt-selection-message-id="b47b8bf0-9151-4637-81cc-c27c479b2746"><div data-selected-text-overlay-target="_r_1t9_" dir="auto" data-markdown-text-style="assistant-message" class="MarkdownRoot-rZKhxa [&amp;&gt;*:first-child]:mt-0 [&amp;&gt;*:last-child]:mb-0 [&amp;&gt;*:last-child]:mb-0 [&amp;&gt;ol:first-child]:mt-0 [&amp;&gt;ul:first-child]:mt-0" style="--markdown-link-color: currentColor;"><div class="my-4 first:mt-0 last:mb-0 empty:hidden" data-dil-source-message-id="b47b8bf0-9151-4637-81cc-c27c479b2746" data-chatgpt-copy-reference="2" data-markdown-copy="contents"><div class="[--entity-prose-inset:0px]"><div hidden=""></div><div class="relative PortalBoundary-TFj9W2 Renderer-ojZscX" data-theme="light" style="--puik-portal-zoom: 1;"><div dir="auto" class="DilRenderer-tB76Jj DilResponseRoot-HfQrEh Reveal-k2IWvM" data-d-direction="col" data-dil-message-id="b47b8bf0-9151-4637-81cc-c27c479b2746"><p class="TextBase-hXhSqg Text-lIMP0_" data-d-text-flow="" data-d-component="text"><span data-d-stream-run="" data-d-text-flow="run" style="--d-stream-ink: rgb(13, 13, 13);">You want a </span><span class="TextBase-hXhSqg Text-lIMP0_" data-d-text-flow="" data-d-component="text" data-d-default-strong="" data-d-inline=""><span data-d-stream-run="" data-d-text-flow="run" style="--d-stream-ink: rgb(13, 13, 13);">complete File Explorer and File Management System inside your website</span></span><span data-d-stream-run="" data-d-text-flow="run" style="--d-stream-ink: rgb(13, 13, 13);">, not just a PDF reader or movie player.</span></p><p class="TextBase-hXhSqg Text-lIMP0_" data-d-text-flow="" data-d-component="text"><span data-d-stream-run="" data-d-text-flow="run" style="--d-stream-ink: rgb(13, 13, 13);">It should work like Windows File Explorer, allowing users to manage, organize, open, preview, edit and download different types of files directly from the website.</span></p><p class="TextBase-hXhSqg Text-lIMP0_" data-d-text-flow="" data-d-component="text"><span data-d-stream-run="" data-d-text-flow="run" style="--d-stream-ink: rgb(13, 13, 13);">Here is the development prompt for Claude Code.</span></p><div data-client-defined-widget="writing_block"><div class="group/writing-block-surface relative isolate w-full min-w-0 overflow-clip rounded-[var(--oai-wb-radius)] [box-shadow:var(--oai-wb-shadow)] [color:var(--oai-wb-text-primary)] [contain:inline-size] [font-family:var(--oai-wb-font-sans)] frame-aD2tvA editorControls-fA0_fZ z-10 clear-both my-4 in-data-[avatar-overlay-orbit-transcript]:my-0 in-data-[avatar-overlay-orbit-transcript]:overflow-y-auto in-data-[avatar-overlay-orbit-transcript]:overscroll-contain in-data-[avatar-overlay-orbit-transcript]:scrollbar-none [--wb-surface-primary:color-mix(in_srgb,var(--color-surface-elevated-secondary)_86%,var(--color-surface))] [--wb-accent:var(--codex-base-accent,var(--color-text-info,var(--color-text)))] [--wb-interactive-background:var(--color-background-primary-ghost-hover)] [--wb-on-accent:var(--color-text-info-solid,var(--color-text-inverse,#fff))] [--wb-selection:var(--color-background-text-selection)] [--wb-font-size:var(--codex-chat-font-size,0.875rem)]" data-oai-writing-block-surface="" data-markdown-copy="rich-block" data-markdown-copy-text="# MASTER PROMPT: COMPLETE WEB-BASED FILE EXPLORER &amp; FILE MANAGEMENT SYSTEM

Act as a senior full-stack developer, file-system architect, document management engineer and UI/UX designer.

Build a complete, professional File Explorer module inside my existing website.

IMPORTANT: I do not want a basic PDF reader, notes viewer or movie player. I want a complete file management platform with the functionality of a modern desktop file explorer.

First inspect my existing project and integrate this module without breaking existing features.

## 1. MAIN OBJECTIVE

Create a complete File Explorer where users can manage all supported files and folders from one interface.

The system should support:
- Documents
- PDF files
- Notes
- Text files
- Word documents
- Excel spreadsheets
- PowerPoint presentations
- Images
- Videos and movies
- Audio and music
- ZIP archives
- Source code files
- JSON, XML and CSV files
- Other common file formats

Do not restrict the system to PDFs and movies.

## 2. FILE EXPLORER INTERFACE

Create a professional desktop-style file manager.

Main layout:

LEFT SIDEBAR:
- Home
- All Files
- Recent Files
- Favorites
- Starred
- Documents
- PDF Documents
- Notes
- Images
- Videos
- Music
- Downloads
- Archives
- Trash
- Shared Files
- Storage Information

TOP TOOLBAR:
- Back
- Forward
- Up one folder
- Refresh
- Breadcrumb navigation
- Search files
- New Folder
- Upload Files
- Upload Folder
- Sort
- Filter
- Grid View
- List View
- Settings

MAIN CONTENT:
- File and folder cards
- File icons and thumbnails
- File names
- File sizes
- File types
- Modified dates
- Selection checkboxes
- Right-click context menu
- Drag-and-drop file management

RIGHT INFORMATION PANEL:
- Selected file preview
- File name
- File type
- Size
- Creation date
- Last modified date
- Location
- File properties

## 3. COMPLETE FILE MANAGEMENT OPERATIONS

Implement real working operations:

1. Create folders.
2. Create subfolders.
3. Upload individual files.
4. Upload multiple files.
5. Upload folders where supported.
6. Download files.
7. Download folders as ZIP archives.
8. Rename files.
9. Rename folders.
10. Copy files.
11. Cut files.
12. Paste files.
13. Move files.
14. Duplicate files.
15. Delete files.
16. Delete folders.
17. Restore deleted files.
18. Permanently delete files.
19. Select multiple files.
20. Bulk operations.
21. Drag and drop files.
22. Add to favorites.
23. Remove from favorites.
24. Sort by name, size, type and date.
25. Search by filename and file type.
26. Filter by file category.
27. View file properties.
28. Show storage usage.

Every operation must work with actual stored files, not just update the interface.

## 4. DOCUMENT VIEWERS

Build an integrated document viewer.

PDF:
- Open PDF files.
- Page navigation.
- Zoom in and out.
- Search within PDF.
- Full-screen reading.
- Download.
- Print.
- Page thumbnails.
- Remember last-read page.

Word:
- Preview DOC and DOCX.
- Support document editing where feasible.
- Download original document.

Excel:
- Preview XLS and XLSX.
- Display worksheets.
- Navigate between sheets.
- Display rows and columns.
- Preserve original files.

PowerPoint:
- Preview PPT and PPTX.
- Slide navigation.
- Full-screen presentation.
- Download original file.

Text:
- Read TXT, MD, LOG and RTF files.
- Search text.
- Copy content.
- Edit and save supported text formats.

CSV:
- Display data in tables.
- Search and filter rows.
- Export and download.

## 5. NOTES MANAGEMENT

Create a built-in Notes Manager.

Features:
- Create notes.
- Edit notes.
- Delete notes.
- Rename notes.
- Auto-save.
- Markdown support.
- Rich-text editor.
- Search notes.
- Organize notes into folders.
- Pin important notes.
- Favorite notes.
- Export notes as TXT, MD or PDF where supported.

Support local autosave and server-side persistence where the backend is configured.

## 6. VIDEO AND MOVIE PLAYER

Build an integrated media player.

Supported formats should include common browser-playable formats such as MP4, WebM and supported audio/video codecs.

Features:
- Video preview thumbnails.
- Play and pause.
- Seek and timeline.
- Volume control.
- Playback speed.
- Full-screen mode.
- Picture-in-picture where supported.
- Subtitle support.
- Resume playback.
- Recently watched.
- Video metadata.
- Search videos.
- Sort by duration and date.

Do not claim every video codec is supported by every browser. Provide an appropriate fallback for unsupported files.

## 7. IMAGE VIEWER

Features:
- Preview images.
- Zoom.
- Rotate.
- Full-screen view.
- Next and previous image.
- Slideshow.
- Image metadata.
- Download original image.

Support JPEG, PNG, WebP, GIF, SVG and other browser-supported formats with safe rendering.

## 8. MUSIC AND AUDIO PLAYER

Features:
- Audio playback.
- Playlist creation.
- Play and pause.
- Next and previous.
- Volume.
- Seek.
- Playback speed.
- Recently played.
- Favorite tracks.
- Album and artist metadata where available.

## 9. ARCHIVE MANAGER

Support:
- ZIP archive inspection.
- List archive contents.
- Extract ZIP files.
- Create ZIP archives.
- Download extracted files.

Validate archive paths and prevent ZIP Slip and archive-bomb attacks.

For unsupported archive formats, show a clear message rather than pretending to extract them.

## 10. ADVANCED SEARCH

Create a powerful file search system.

Search by:
- File name.
- File extension.
- File type.
- Folder.
- File size.
- Creation date.
- Modified date.
- File contents for supported indexed formats.

Include:
- Instant search.
- Search suggestions.
- Recent searches.
- Advanced filters.
- Search results grouped by file category.

## 11. STORAGE AND FILE SECURITY

Implement:
- Storage usage dashboard.
- File size tracking.
- Upload progress.
- Download progress.
- Upload cancellation.
- File size limits.
- Allowed file type configuration.
- File validation.
- Authentication.
- Role-based permissions.
- Per-user file ownership.
- Private file access.
- Secure download authorization.
- Audit logs.
- Trash retention and recovery.

Never expose private files through predictable public URLs.

Prevent:
- Path traversal.
- Unauthorized file access.
- Malicious uploads.
- Unsafe archive extraction.
- Executing uploaded files.
- Cross-user file access.

## 12. STORAGE ARCHITECTURE

Use the existing backend and database if present.

Support an extensible storage architecture:
- Local server storage.
- Object storage such as S3-compatible storage.
- Cloud storage adapters where configured.

Store file metadata in the database and file contents in the configured storage backend.

Suggested database entities:
- User
- File
- Folder
- FileVersion
- Favorite
- FileShare
- FilePermission
- TrashItem
- RecentFile
- AuditLog

Implement file ownership, folder hierarchy, permissions and safe storage paths.

## 13. LOCAL COMPUTER FILE ACCESS

Important browser limitation:

A website cannot silently access every file on a visitor's computer.

Implement:
- Standard file upload using the browser file picker.
- Folder upload where supported.
- Drag-and-drop upload.
- File System Access API where supported and explicitly authorized.
- Download to the user's device.
- Permission-aware local folder access.

Never attempt to bypass browser security or access unauthorized computer files.

Clearly distinguish between:
1. Files stored in the website.
2. Files selected from the user's local computer.
3. Files stored in connected cloud storage.

## 14. UI/UX DESIGN

Design the file manager with:
- Professional dark and light themes.
- Modern desktop file explorer layout.
- Responsive mobile interface.
- Grid and list views.
- File-type icons.
- File thumbnails.
- Context menus.
- Keyboard shortcuts.
- Breadcrumb navigation.
- Smooth animations.
- Upload progress indicators.
- Empty states.
- Loading states.
- Error messages.
- Confirmation dialogs.

The interface should feel like a combination of Windows File Explorer and a modern cloud drive.

## 15. API AND BACKEND

Create appropriate APIs for:
- File listing.
- Folder creation.
- File upload.
- File download.
- Rename.
- Copy.
- Move.
- Delete.
- Restore.
- Search.
- File metadata.
- Favorites.
- Storage analytics.
- File previews.
- File permissions.
- Sharing.

Use authenticated and authorized endpoints.

Implement pagination for large directories and streaming for large file uploads/downloads.

## 16. DEVELOPMENT PHASES

Phase 1: Inspect the existing website and identify the technology stack.

Phase 2: Design the file explorer UI.

Phase 3: Implement folder and file storage.

Phase 4: Implement complete file management operations.

Phase 5: Implement document readers and viewers.

Phase 6: Implement notes, image, audio and video viewers.

Phase 7: Implement ZIP management.

Phase 8: Implement search, favorites, history and storage analytics.

Phase 9: Implement authentication and permissions.

Phase 10: Test every operation and file type.

Phase 11: Optimize performance and prepare production deployment.

## 17. FINAL ACCEPTANCE REQUIREMENTS

The module must:
- Work inside my existing website.
- Manage real uploaded files.
- Create and manage folder hierarchies.
- Read PDFs and documents.
- Create and manage notes.
- Play supported movies and audio.
- Preview images.
- Manage ZIP files.
- Search and organize files.
- Support bulk operations.
- Work on desktop and mobile.
- Protect private user files.
- Preserve files across page reloads and sessions.
- Handle errors and unsupported formats correctly.

Deliver complete source code, database changes, APIs, installation instructions, environment configuration, and testing documentation.

Do not create a visual-only prototype. Do not use fake data for completed operations. Do not remove existing functionality.

Start by inspecting the repository and implement this as a fully integrated File Explorer module." data-testid="chatgpt-writing-block" data-writing-block-variant="document" style="--oai-wb-spacing: var(--spacing,0.25rem); --oai-wb-text-primary: var(--wb-text-primary,var(--color-token-text-primary,var(--text-primary,#0d0d0d))); --oai-wb-text-secondary: var(--wb-text-secondary,var(--color-token-text-secondary,var(--text-secondary,#5d5d5d))); --oai-wb-text-tertiary: var(--wb-text-tertiary,var(--color-token-text-tertiary,var(--text-tertiary,#8f8f8f))); --oai-wb-surface-primary: var(--wb-surface-primary,var(--color-token-main-surface-primary,var(--main-surface-primary,#fff))); --oai-wb-surface-secondary: var(--wb-surface-secondary,var(--color-token-bg-tertiary,var(--main-surface-secondary,#f5f5f5))); --oai-wb-interactive-secondary-hover: var(--wb-interactive-secondary-hover,var(--color-token-interactive-bg-secondary-hover,var(--oai-wb-surface-secondary))); --oai-wb-border: var(--wb-border,var(--color-token-border,var(--border-light,rgb(0 0 0/8%)))); --oai-wb-border-hover: var(--wb-border-hover,var(--color-token-border-default,var(--border-medium,rgb(0 0 0/12%)))); --oai-wb-divider: var(--wb-divider,var(--color-token-border-light,var(--border-light,rgb(0 0 0/5%)))); --oai-wb-focus: var(--wb-focus,var(--color-token-focus-border,var(--border-strong,#5b9dd9))); --oai-wb-control-border: var(--wb-control-border,var(--interactive-border-focus,var(--oai-wb-focus))); --oai-wb-entity-accent: var(--wb-entity-accent,var(--theme-entity-accent,var(--oai-wb-accent))); --oai-wb-accent: var(--wb-accent,var(--interactive-label-accent-default,#0285ff)); --oai-wb-on-accent: var(--wb-on-accent,var(--bg-primary,#fff)); --oai-wb-interactive-background: var(--wb-interactive-background,var(--interactive-bg-accent-default,color-mix(in srgb,#0285ff 12%,transparent))); --oai-wb-selection: var(--wb-selection,var(--theme-user-selection-bg,var(--selection,#93c5fd))); --oai-wb-radius: var(--wb-radius,1